        "narrative": "<p>The lake trout catch in 1998 was within the normal range for lakes of this class, and it was similar to past catches in this lake.  No lake trout younger than five years were collected; however, that is not unusual in natural lake trout lakes.  Lake trout growth had been about average for the area, with a forage base that seemed to consist mostly of invertebrates, with some access to burbot and yellow perch.The northern pike catch was also within the normal range, and similar to past catches.  Several northern pike over 25 inches were collected, with relatively fast growth accounting for the presence of good numbers of large fish.  No northern pike older than five years were collected, but five-year-old (almost six year old) fish averaged 28.6 inches in length when captured in September.No walleye or smallmouth bass were collected, and none have ever been reported from this lake.  They are not native to this area.</p>",
